@startuml replication-overview
title AISafe - Replication and consistency per service (eventual consistency, AP)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 40
left to right direction

rectangle "Flight Operations\n(2 or 3 replicas)" as FO {
  component "replica A" as FA
  component "replica B" as FB
}
rectangle "Airports & Routes\n(2 or 3 replicas)" as AR {
  component "replica A" as RA
  component "replica B" as RB
}
rectangle "Aircraft\n(2 or 3 replicas)" as AC {
  component "replica A" as CA
  component "replica B" as CB
}
rectangle "Maintenance\n(2 or 3 replicas)" as MT {
  component "replica A" as MA
  component "replica B" as MB
}

FA <--> FB
RA <--> RB
CA <--> CB
MA <--> MB

note right of FB
  Flight Operations: a write is copied synchronously to at least one peer
  and to the others in the background; pending copies are retried every 5 s;
  a restarted replica syncs from its peers; the newest revision wins.
end note
note right of RB
  Airports & Routes: replication outbox with retry every 5 s
  (up to about 5 s of inconsistency); a GET that misses is
  forwarded to the peers (header X-P2P-Hops limits the hops).
end note
note right of CB
  Aircraft: asynchronous copy of each write to the peers;
  a GET that misses locally is forwarded to the peers.
end note
note right of MB
  Maintenance: maintenance records and templates are replicated
  by global id (revision, retry every 5 s, sync on startup).
end note
@enduml
